{"step_index":22,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T09:35:40Z","content":"I hear you — no vidIQ, we'll keep it fast and direct. \n\nSince you're studying for a GTU mid-sem, you don't want long 2-hour university lectures (like NPTEL). You need exam-oriented Indian creators who get straight to the point, solve numericals step-by-step, and explain derivations simply.\n\nHere is your exact Tier 1 battle plan. I've broken down exactly what to type into YouTube and which creators are best for each specific topic.\n\n### 🔴 Tier 1 Topics — Your YouTube Watch List\n\n| Topic (from your Mid-Sem) | What to search on YouTube (Copy-Paste this) | Best YouTubers to watch for this |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **General Cartesian Eq. Derivation** | `\"general heat conduction equation in cartesian coordinates derivation\"` | **Tikle's Academy** (Best for step-by-step derivations) or **Mechanical Engineering 4u** |\n| **Fourier's Law & Thermal Diffusivity** | `\"fourier's law of heat conduction and thermal diffusivity\"` | **Neso Academy** (Clean, visual, perfect for theory) |\n| **Composite Wall (Theory + Numerical)** | `\"heat conduction through composite wall numerical\"` | **Tikle's Academy** (Watch one numerical video, he covers the resistance concept perfectly) |\n| **Critical Radius of Insulation** | `\"critical radius of insulation cylinder sphere derivation\"` | **Gate Academy Plus** or **Unacademy GATE** (They explain *why* it happens very well) |\n| **Fins (Theory + Insulated Tip Eq)** | `\"heat transfer through fins insulated at tip derivation\"` | **Tikle's Academy** (Highly recommended for the fin derivations) |\n| **Fin Numericals** | `\"fin heat transfer numerical problems\"` | **Tikle's Academy** (He solves the exact GTU-style problems) |\n| **Dimensionless Numbers (Re, Nu, Pr, Gr)** | `\"dimensionless numbers in convection heat transfer\"` | **Neso Academy** or **Tutorials Point** (Keep it short, you just need definitions and physical significance) |\n| **Free vs Forced Convection** | `\"difference between free and forced convection\"` | **Tutorials Point** or any short 3-minute summary video |\n\n### Recommended Strategy for YouTube Study:\n1. **For Derivations & Numericals (The heavy 7-mark questions):** Go straight to **Tikle's Academy**. His videos are literally structured like university exam answers.\n2. **For Theory & Definitions (The 3-4 mark questions):** Use **Neso Academy**. Their videos are shorter, highly visual, and easier to digest.\n3. **Watch on 1.5x Speed:** You have ~8 topics here. At 1.5x speed, you can get through the core material in about 3-4 hours. \n\nDo you want to start with the **General Cartesian Equation derivation** video, or jump straight into **Composite Walls**? Let me know which one you're tackling first.","thinking":"**Defining Tier 1 Topics**\n\nI'm now focusing on identifying Tier 1 topics suitable for Indian engineering students, specifically within the GTU context. I'll need to generate effective search queries and recommend relevant YouTubers. I've ruled out using vidiq. I'm exploring an alternate approach now.\n\n\n**Generating Topic Searches**\n\nI've transitioned from identifying Tier 1 topics to formulating precise search queries, given these are foundational mechanical engineering concepts. It appears several are basic concepts such as Fourier's law, and dimensionless numbers, and I can bypass agent-based YouTube scraping. I am also thinking about providing the user with specific search terms and key YouTubers like Tikle's Academy and NPTEL.\n\n\n"}
